[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"265","stub":{"id":"265","section":"Pit 5: Pit 5 Dam to Pit 5 Powerhouse","altname":"Pit 5 Run","river":"Pit","difficulty":"IV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"437","dateTime":"2026-05-11T23:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Madesi River Access below Pit 5 Dam on river left has a river access point, bathrooms, and camping.","id":"112851","location":{"latitude":"40.996322","longitude":"-121.872758"},"name":"Madesi River Access at Pit 5 Dam Put-in","distance":"0","photoID":"888138","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid is right below the put-in. The channel in this rapid is braided and full of vegetation. The middle channel seems best, but this could change in the future.","id":"102467","location":{"latitude":"40.996857","longitude":"-121.872927"},"name":"African Queen","distance":"0.04","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"888139"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Chunky boulder-strewn rapid. It can be difficult to scout and is the hardest rapid on the run. A sneak is available on the far left.","id":"102456","location":{"latitude":"40.994068","longitude":"-121.875819"},"name":"Sneak Peek","distance":"0.3","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":"882319"},{"type":"rapid","description":"A natural river wide dam","id":"102457","location":{"latitude":"41.001702","longitude":"-121.880858"},"name":"Upper Ledge","distance":"1.02","difficulty":"III+","approximate":true,"photoID":"882197"},{"type":"rapid","description":"River Wide Playspot","id":"102466","location":{"latitude":"41.001428","longitude":"-121.881769"},"name":"Spin City","distance":"1.07","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false,"photoID":"882322"},{"type":"rapid","description":null,"id":"102458","location":{"latitude":"41.000425","longitude":"-121.884071"},"name":"Spillway ","distance":"1.21","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"40233"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Braided at the top.  Long Class III +","id":"102465","location":{"latitude":"41.006328","longitude":"-121.885527"},"name":"Kinner","distance":"1.71","difficulty":"III+","approximate":true,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"access","description":"Access at this intermediate access point is on river right just downstream of the bridge in Big Bend. The river has more challenging class IV whitewater upstream of this access point, but is only class III below this bridge.","id":"6603","location":{"latitude":"41.020678","longitude":"-121.910574"},"name":"Big Bend Bridge","distance":"3.72","photoID":"0","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"This is a long Class III immediately below Big Bend. This rapid is compicated by the fact that much of the water pushes into the overhanging vegitation on the right bank.","id":"102459","location":{"latitude":"41.02086","longitude":"-121.913917"},"name":"Bad Alder","distance":"3.92","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"882320"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Long Class III, Hot Springs are at the bottom of this rapid on the left. The river braids at the top of this rapid.  The left channel is generally the best.","id":"102460","location":{"latitude":"41.023146","longitude":"-121.918781"},"name":"Hot Springs ","distance":"4.37","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"882427"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Long Class III","id":"102461","location":{"latitude":"41.025131","longitude":"-121.925742"},"name":"Osprey","distance":"4.8","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid is below where Kosk Creek comes in on the right.  One of the prettiest parts of the river.","id":"102462","location":{"latitude":"41.026353","longitude":"-121.933295"},"name":"Kosk Creek","distance":"5.33","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"882203"},{"type":"takeout","description":"The take-out is on river left across the river from the James B. Black Powerhouse (aka Pit 5 Powerhouse). The access site has a large parking area and bathroom.","id":"118132","location":{"latitude":"40.991516","longitude":"-121.97473"},"name":"Pit 5 Powerhouse Take-Out","distance":"9.25","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101254849","title":null,"post_date":"2020-06-18 04:00:00+00","detail":"In the first rapid below Big Bend, known as Bad Alder, there is a large Alder spanning the channel (just a case of a rapid living up to its name). The tree is virtually impossible to avoid and it would be very easy to get swept into it during release flows. The good news is that there is a side channel to the right of the main channel that looks like it will be runable at release flows. This channel should be pretty easy to scout from the parking area.","user":{"name":"Theresa Lorejo-Simsiman"}}],"photos":[{"id":"888138","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890907","description":"Unusable boat ramp build by PG&E.  Use of the ramp puts paddlers at the top of an unrunnable chute.","caption":"Madesi Boat Ramp","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/888138","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/888138"}},{"id":"0eePL5YwwIjrlv6R2ddfd","ext":"jpg","post_id":"6rH2t3Av0vyCzv3VNZCGq","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Jeff Venturino","poi_id":"102458","photo_date":"2013-04-14T18:18:04.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T18:18:04.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/0eePL5YwwIjrlv6R2ddfd","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/0eePL5YwwIjrlv6R2ddfd"}},{"id":"882323","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885026","description":"One of the many Class IV rapids on the Pit 5 reach of the Pi